With a busy pet and a bad situation, try robbing the
shop from within.

This takes advantage of the niggling discrepency
that _you_ are not outside the shop until you
step out the door (I've even jumped past the
shopkeeper into the doorway and not triggered the
Kop swarm), but a shop item is outside the shop on
the first square just inside the doorway.

So, from within, and with the company of the
shopkeeper and your friendly neighborhood
kleptomaniac pet Fluffy:

1) Shut and if possible lock the shop door to limit
interruptions from anything that can't crawl under
the door or break it down or whatever, and to keep
Fluffy inside the shop.

2) Stand on the second square directly into the shop
as seen from the doorway, resting or searching.

The shopkeeper will dance around a lot.

Your pet will dance around a lot.

3) Every once in a while, your pet will drop some item
on that one square that counts as "outside".  Step
forward, where the item is out of the shop but you
are "in" the shop for Kop calling purposes, pick
the item up, step "back into" the shop, and sell the
item to the shopkeeper.

Every once in a while some monster will slither
under the door or be created in the shop, giving
your pet a chance to kill and eat something.

Sooner or later you'll have all the money and the
shopkeeper will be filing for bankruptcy.

You can alternate this with buying the stuff from
the shop that you really want and either holding
onto it or setting it outside the door, if you like.

